# Forge Foresight — every variable this service reads, and nothing else.
#
# Rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2: a repository declares the variables it needs and the deploy
# provides exactly those. This file IS that declaration, and `src/env.ts` is the only place any of
# them is spelled. `env_file: .env` fan-out — one file handed to every container — is what put the
# custody master secret inside the marketing site, and it has nothing to justify it.
#
# EVERY SECRET HERE IS LEFT EMPTY, NOT FILLED WITH A PLACEHOLDER, so a copy of this file cannot
# boot: a placeholder that starts is a placeholder that reaches production. They used to say
# `CHANGE_ME`, which was refused only because a deny-list happened to contain that exact string —
# and a deny-list cannot contain the next placeholder somebody writes. micro-org #142's
# `estate-only-outbox-secret-00000000000000` is 40 characters and was on nobody's list.
#
# `env.ts` now runs `@cloudsforge/secrets`, which asserts SHAPE instead, per class of secret:
#
#     OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET        base64 or hex, 32 decoded BYTES, entropy floor
#                                  → openssl rand -base64 48
#     FORESIGHT_IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL / FORESIGHT_SERVICE_TOKEN
#                                  → a `cfsc_…` minted by identity (estate-bootstrap.sh). A JWT is
#                                    refused BY NAME: it dies ten minutes after the boot that read
#                                    it, which is micro-org #222.
#     FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_TOKEN / FORESIGHT_SEARCH_TOKEN
#                                  → OPAQUE. Their alphabets belong to their vendors, so only the
#                                    placeholder markers and a low floor are asserted. Absent is a
#                                    supported mode and is how every deployment runs today.
#
# There is no CI branch, no NODE_ENV exemption and no way to opt out, deliberately.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the process
PORT=4021
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Names this replica in `jobs.locked_by`. The container id under compose, the pod name under
# Kubernetes — in both cases the thing an operator searches for after finding a stuck lease.
INSTANCE_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the ONE database
# Rule 1: a service owns exactly one database and reads no other. CI greps the source for a second
# connection-string variable, so adding one fails the build rather than review.
FORESIGHT_DATABASE_URL=postgres://foresight:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/foresight
FORESIGHT_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── identity
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=http://127.0.0.1:4001

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── upstreams
# The scoped service credential. NEVER a shared one — SD-05. The scopes this token needs are
# `custody:sign:deployer`, `custody:address:create`, `indexer:read`, `indexer:write`,
# `ledger:post`, `policy:decide` and — only where a house seed is configured — `admin:read`,
# and no more.
FORESIGHT_SERVICE_TOKEN=
CUSTODY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4005
INDEXER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4008
LEDGER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4007
POLICY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4006
FORESIGHT_UPSTREAM_DEADLINE_MS=5000
FORESIGHT_POLICY_DEADLINE_MS=3000

# The action staking is decided under. `micro-policy`'s registry is CLOSED — an unregistered name
# is a 400, not a guess — and there is no `foresight.stake` in it yet. `trade.order.place` is the
# registered action whose description actually fits. Move this the day policy gains its own.
FORESIGHT_POLICY_ACTION=trade.order.place

# HMAC key for outbound event signatures, so a subscriber can prove an event came from us.
OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the house seed (doc 21 §5)
# BOTH MAY BE ABSENT, AND ABSENT IS A SUPPORTED MODE: this deployment runs no engagement
# programme, and approving a market with `houseSeedPerOutcomeWei` refuses with a sentence saying
# so rather than silently seeding nothing.
#
# The published platform address the house seed stakes from. It is an ORDINARY BETTOR's address:
# it stakes through the same `stake(uint8)` everyone uses, its position is mirrored like anyone's,
# and its winnings return through `claim()` like anyone's. Its key lives OUTSIDE this estate's
# custody — custody has no transaction shape that can call a contract with value (see
# `src/houseseed.ts`) — and it is published the way the platform miners' coinbase addresses are.
FORESIGHT_HOUSE_ADDRESS=
# micro-admin-api, for reading the engagement caps at approval time. The service token needs the
# EXACT scope `admin:read` — admin-api matches scopes exactly (§3.3h), so `admin:*` will not do.
ADMIN_API_URL=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the custodial stake (the second way to bet)
# The published platform address the CUSTODIAL pool share is staked from — a bet paid for with
# coins already deposited with CloudsForge, no browser wallet anywhere in it. Like the house seed
# above it is an ordinary bettor's address whose key lives outside this estate's custody, for the
# same reason: custody cannot call a contract with value.
#
# ABSENT IS THE SUPPORTED MODE, AND IT IS THE MODE EVERY ESTATE IS IN. `server.ts` derives
# `custodialStakingAvailable` from this and nothing else, so unset means `GET /stake-assets`
# reports the feature off and `CustodialStakePanel` renders nothing at all.
#
# DO NOT SET IT WITHOUT READING THIS. `src/custodialstakes.ts` exports the whole lifecycle —
# `markStaked`, `markRefunded`, `markSettled`, `escrowPostings`, `refundPostings`,
# `settlementPostings`, `aggregateShares` — and `server.ts` calls exactly one of them,
# `acceptStake`. A stake therefore reaches `accepted`, which moves the bettor's coins from
# available to escrow, and stops: nothing stakes it on chain, nothing refunds it, nothing settles
# it. Setting this address today opens an intake that strands strangers' money. The lifecycle
# routes come first.
FORESIGHT_CUSTODIAL_ADDRESS=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the header image (micro-studio)
# WHERE A BROWSER CAN REACH micro-studio. Used for exactly one thing: composing the `bytesUrl` a
# client puts in `<img src>` for a market's or an idea's header image.
#
# NOT `STUDIO_URL`, and the different name is the point. `tessera/.env.example:73` has `STUDIO_URL`
# and it is a SERVER-TO-SERVER address — in the estate it resolves to a container name on a private
# compose network, which no browser can reach. Setting that value here would mint image URLs that
# exist only inside the cluster: a broken picture on the user's page and a green health check
# everywhere else. foresight makes no server-to-server call to studio at all (it holds a reference
# and authorises it; it never fetches bytes and never recomputes a checksum), so there is nothing
# here for a `STUDIO_URL` to do.
#
# Must be an ORIGIN — scheme and host, no path, no trailing slash. A path segment would produce
# `…/studio/v1/assets/…`, which fails as a broken image rather than at boot, so it is refused at
# boot instead.
#
# ABSENT IS A SUPPORTED MODE and is the estate's current state: the compose publishes studio on
# 127.0.0.1:4111 with no public hostname, and `studio` has no row in the @cloudsforge/ui surfaces
# registry. Unset, every `image.bytesUrl` is null — "this deployment cannot tell you where the
# bytes are" — rather than a relative path that would resolve against foresight's own origin and
# 404. The estate has written that lesson down once already: the compose leaves
# `STUDIO_ASSET_BASE_URL` unset because a base URL there "would mint storageUrls that look fetchable
# and 404 — a zero wearing a status code".
#
# Uploads go from the CLIENT to studio directly, as raw image bytes to
# `POST /v1/uploads?visibility=public`. Public matters: studio's bytes route needs no Authorization
# header for a public asset, and a browser sends none on an `<img src>`.
# STUDIO_PUBLIC_URL=https://studio.cloudsforge.online

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the chain
# `chain -> JSON-RPC endpoint`, as JSON. EMPTY BY DEFAULT, and empty means a deploy is refused
# rather than falling back to a public node nobody chose.
FORESIGHT_RPC_URLS={"ember":"http://127.0.0.1:8545"}
FORESIGHT_RPC_DEADLINE_MS=5000

# TWO deliberate settings are needed to reach a mainnet, and this is why: a market on a mainnet
# holds real EMBER belonging to strangers, and one typo in FORESIGHT_NETWORK must not be enough.
FORESIGHT_NETWORK=testnet
FORESIGHT_MAINNET_ENABLED=false

# Where the settlement fee goes. Bound into every market contract at deploy time and unchangeable
# afterwards, so a wrong value here is a fee stream nobody can collect.
FORESIGHT_TREASURY_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# The custody-held address that may resolve or void a market. It is a `deployer`-purpose custody
# key: it can sign a zero-value contract creation and NOTHING ELSE, which is why the resolution is
# posted as a one-shot contract. See `src/resolve.ts`. The user id and order id are custody's
# binding for it and must match the row custody holds, character for character.
FORESIGHT_ORACLE_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
FORESIGHT_ORACLE_USER_ID=foresight
FORESIGHT_ORACLE_ORDER_ID=oracle-ember-testnet

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── market defaults
# Basis points of the LOSING pool taken on settlement. A winner therefore never receives less than
# they staked. Hard-capped at 1000 (10%) by the contract itself.
FORESIGHT_DEFAULT_FEE_BPS=200
# 24 hours: long enough for a wrong resolution to be noticed by somebody who was asleep, short
# enough that a correct one does not feel like a withheld payment.
FORESIGHT_DEFAULT_DISPUTE_WINDOW_SECONDS=86400

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── deploy and gas
FORESIGHT_DEPLOYS_ENABLED=true
FORESIGHT_MIN_GAS_PRICE_WEI=1000000000
FORESIGHT_MAX_GAS_PRICE_WEI=500000000000
FORESIGHT_DEPLOY_GAS_LIMIT=3000000
FORESIGHT_RESOLVE_GAS_LIMIT=300000
FORESIGHT_STUCK_MINUTES=30

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the idea pipeline (optional)
# ALL FOUR MAY BE ABSENT, AND ABSENT IS A SUPPORTED MODE. The pipeline records "no proposals" and
# the operator queue stays empty; nothing crashes and nothing logs an error every six hours for a
# thing nobody has configured. An operator can write every market question by hand — `POST /ideas`
# is the same path — so a service that fell over without its suggester would have the dependency
# exactly backwards. `micro-notify`'s SMTP discipline.
FORESIGHT_SEARCH_URL=
FORESIGHT_SEARCH_TOKEN=
FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_URL=
FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_TOKEN=
FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_MODEL_ID=
FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_DEADLINE_MS=30000
FORESIGHT_PROPOSER_BATCH_SIZE=5

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jobs
# There is no `setInterval` in this repository — rule 8, and CI greps for one. Recurrence is a
# leased job that re-enqueues itself, which is the only form that is correct with two replicas.
FORESIGHT_LEASE_MS=60000
FORESIGHT_JOB_POLL_MS=1000
FORESIGHT_PROPOSE_EVERY_MINUTES=360

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── tests
# Read by `src/testsupport.ts`. The name MUST contain "test": the harness truncates every table
# this service owns and refuses a database whose name does not say what it is.
# FORESIGHT_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://foresight:foresight@127.0.0.1:55460/foresight_test
